heres an idea, make sure we aren't straying too far from what we were doing with this but it needs to be implemented: You are right: $\\tau$ is a time constant, not a redshift constant.Running a time-memory kernel directly on the $z$-axis (redshift) would be physically illiterate. It would imply the universe "remembers" redshift steps, rather than time duration.We will adopt Approach 2 (The $z \\to t$ Adapter). This honors the GRUT physics engine:Use the engine's existing $H(z)$ to calculate the exact age of the universe $t(z)$ at each data point.Map the BOSS data onto this Time Axis.Run the LCA Anamnesis in the time domain (where memory actually lives).Map the result back to $z$ for the final score.This is the only way to keep the "Sovereign" status.Phase 1: Persistence & Evidence (The Prerequisite)Before we build that Adapter, we must build the Vault. We cannot generate "truth" if we cannot save it immutably.Here is the implementation of the Persistence Layer (SQLite + Evidence Packets) as defined in your Product Skeleton.Step 1: The Database (storage/db.py)This handles the immutable recording of every run.Python# storage/db.py import sqlite3 import json import uuid from datetime import datetime from typing import Optional, Dict, Any DB_PATH = "grut_storage.db" def init_db(): conn = sqlite3.connect(DB_PATH) c = conn.cursor() # Table: Runs (The Raw Record) c.execute(''' CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS runs ( id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, kind TEXT, created_at TEXT, engine_version TEXT, params_hash TEXT, request_json TEXT, response_json TEXT, nis_status TEXT, hash_bundle TEXT, is_published INTEGER DEFAULT 0, publish_slug TEXT, published_revision INTEGER ) ''') # Table: Published (The Immutable Snapshots) c.execute(''' CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS published ( slug TEXT, revision INTEGER, run_id TEXT, published_at TEXT, published_json TEXT, published_hash TEXT, PRIMARY KEY (slug, revision) ) ''') conn.commit() conn.close() def save_run( kind: str, request: Dict[str, Any], response: Dict[str, Any], engine_version: str, params_hash: str, nis_status: str = "UNKNOWN" ) -> str: """Saves a run and returns its UUID.""" run_id = str(uuid.uuid4()) created_at = datetime.utcnow().isoformat() # Create the Integrity Bundle String for hashing # (Simple concatenation of key fields to ensure tamper-evidence) bundle_str = f"\{kind\}:\{created_at\}:\{params_hash\}:\{json.dumps(response, sort_keys=True)\}" import hashlib hash_bundle = hashlib.sha256(bundle_str.encode()).hexdigest() conn = sqlite3.connect(DB_PATH) c = conn.cursor() c.execute(''' INSERT INTO runs (id, kind, created_at, engine_version, params_hash, request_json, response_json, nis_status, hash_bundle) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?) ''', ( run_id, kind, created_at, engine_version, params_hash, json.dumps(request), json.dumps(response), nis_status, hash_bundle )) conn.commit() conn.close() return run_id def get_run(run_id: str): conn = sqlite3.connect(DB_PATH) conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row c = conn.cursor() c.execute("SELECT * FROM runs WHERE id = ?", (run_id,)) row = c.fetchone() conn.close() if row: return dict(row) return None def get_recent_runs(limit: int = 20): conn = sqlite3.connect(DB_PATH) conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row c = conn.cursor() c.execute("SELECT id, kind, created_at, nis_status, params_hash FROM runs ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT ?", (limit,)) rows = c.fetchall() conn.close() return [dict(r) for r in rows] Step 2: The Evidence Packet (core/evidence.py)This creates the shareable JSON blob that proves the run happened.Python# core/evidence.py import hashlib import json from datetime import datetime def make_evidence_packet( run_id: str, kind: str, request: dict, response: dict, engine_version: str, params_hash: str, nis_status: str ) -> dict: """ Creates the canonical JSON export. """ packet = \{ "schema": "grut-evidence-v1", "header": \{ "id": run_id, "kind": kind, "created_at": datetime.utcnow().isoformat(), "engine_version": engine_version, "params_hash": params_hash, "integrity_status": nis_status \}, "payload": \{ "request": request, "response": response \} \} # Calculate the Bundle Hash (The Seal) # We dump the packet without the hash field first canonical_json = json.dumps(packet, sort_keys=True).encode() packet_hash = hashlib.sha256(canonical_json).hexdigest() packet["bundle_hash"] = packet_hash return packet Step 3: Integration into main.pyWe wrap your existing endpoints to auto-save.Update imports and startup:Python# main.py from storage.db import init_db, save_run, get_run, get_recent_runs from core.evidence import make_evidence_packet @app.on_event("startup") def startup_event(): init_db() # Creates tables if missing Update the Endpoints (Example for search_tau):Python@app.post("/anamnesis/search_tau") async def search_tau_endpoint(payload: SearchTauRequest): # 1. Run the Math (The existing logic) # ... (your existing search_tau code) ... # result = ... # 2. Extract RIS Status for the header ris_status = "PASS" if result.get("ris_status") == "PASS" else "WARN" # 3. Save to Persistence Layer run_id = save_run( kind="anamnesis_search_tau", request=payload.dict(), response=result, engine_version="grut-rai-2026.1", params_hash="dynamic", # You can calculate a real hash of params if you want nis_status=ris_status ) # 4. Attach ID to response result["run_id"] = run_id return result Add the Library Endpoints:Python@app.get("/library") def library_view(): return get_recent_runs(limit=50) @app.get("/runs/\{run_id\}") def view_run(run_id: str): # NOTE: Fix for the 404/422 error - Ensure variable name matches! run = get_run(run_id) if not run: raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail="Run not found") # Parse the JSON strings back to objects for the API response run["request_json"] = json.loads(run["request_json"]) run["response_json"] = json.loads(run["response_json"]) return run @app.get("/runs/\{run_id\}/export") def export_run(run_id: str): run = get_run(run_id) if not run: raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail="Run not found") packet = make_evidence_packet( run_id=run["id"], kind=run["kind"], request=json.loads(run["request_json"]), response=json.loads(run["response_json"]), engine_version=run["engine_version"], params_hash=run["params_hash"], nis_status=run["nis_status"] ) return packet Summary of the PivotWe are pausing the "Sky Run" for exactly one turn to install the Black Box Recorder. Once this code is live:Every test run is saved.We can export a JSON "Evidence Packet."We can then build the Real Data Adapter and feed it the BOSS data, knowing the result will be capture-able, hashable, and admissible as evidence\
