Perfect! Publishing v1 implemented: backend + evidence packet header + API endpoints + UI + tests. All tests pass locally (25 passed, 33 warnings). Below is a concise summary of what I changed and how to use it. 
\f9 \uc0\u55357 \u56615 
\f0  What I implemented 1) DB layer (storage/db.py) 
\f9 \uc0\u9989 
\f0  Added robust publishing helpers: create_or_update_publish(run_id) \'97 creates a deterministic, immutable published snapshot (slug, revision, published_json, published_hash) and returns metadata including url_latest and url_revision. get_published_latest(slug) and get_published_revision(slug, revision) wrappers. Slug generation: make_slug creates readable slug from kind, params_hash[:8], and bundle_hash[:8]. Sanitizes to URL-safe [a-z0-9-] and appends -2, -3 if needed to avoid collisions. Schema migration: Ensures published table uses composite primary key (slug, revision). If older legacy schema present (slug primary key only), runs a migration copying rows into a new table. Stores canonical published JSON using canonical serialization (sort_keys + separators), and published hash as SHA256 of canonical JSON. get_topic() and list_runs() now provide publish metadata (is_published, publish_slug, published_revision). 2) Evidence packet format (core/evidence.py) 
\f9 \uc0\u9989 
\f0  New schema: grut-evidence-v1. Packet contains: schema: "grut-evidence-v1" header: \{ id, kind, created_at, engine_version, params_hash, status, bundle_hash \} request, response, receipt Backward-compat fields: metadata and top-level bundle_hash (keeps old code/tests happy) Deterministic canonical hashing for bundle_hash (header-without-bundle_hash + request + receipt using canonical JSON). verify_evidence_packet supports both legacy and new formats. 3) API (api/main.py) 
\f9 \uc0\u9989 
\f0  POST /runs/\{run_id\}/publish Uses create_or_update_publish(run_id); returns slug, revision, published_hash, published_at, public_url. Returns structured error JSON on failure (does not crash). GET /p/\{slug\} (public) Returns sanitized public snapshot with only \{metadata, request, response, receipt, bundle_hash\} (prevents internal path leakage). GET /p/\{slug\}/\{revision\} Returns sanitized snapshot for specific revision. GET /p/\{slug\}/info and GET /p/\{slug\}/\{revision\}/info Return publishing metadata + the full evidence packet (admin view). Existing library endpoints now surface publish metadata via list_runs(). 4) UI (ui/index.html) 
\f9 \uc0\u9989 
\f0  Library: Publish button present in each run row (unchanged; improved behavior). After Publish, share link is copied and UI refreshes library and topic view. GRUTipedia: Each related run now shows: Export button Publish button (if not published) Open Published button (if published) Share link (if published) Small modal viewer to open a published snapshot (header + receipt) and export the JSON. UI state: lastRunId tracking and unambiguous "Link last run" behavior (captured earlier). 5) Tests (tests/test_publish.py and adjustments) 
\f9 \uc0\u9989 
